  "verdict": "INTERVENE3 \u2014 paralog synthetic lethality as a DRUGGED route around cancer undruggability. G1 PASS: the DepMap conditional SL test (expr-tertile-conditioned differential dependency, NOT co-dependency correlation) recovers 9/12 (75%) of a frozen external curated known-paralog-SL set at BH-FDR<0.1 + Cliff's-delta<=-0.1, vs a paralog-universe base rate of 7.8% (10x) and a random non-paralog-pair null of 7.4%. The SL signal is REAL and recovered above both nulls. G2 (descriptive) \u2014 of INTERVENE2's 3416 UNDRUGGED validated selective dependencies, 1077 have any paralog partner, 406 have a DepMap-validated paralog-SL partner, and 25 (0.7%) have an SL partner that IS drugged in ChEMBL (16=0.5% with an APPROVED-drug partner). So paralog-SL opens an existing-drug ROUTE HYPOTHESIS to ~1% of the otherwise-undruggable validated dependencies (driver subset: 3/192). SCOPE: this is an IN-SILICO GENETIC-INTERACTION HYPOTHESIS for a combination/context experiment, NOT a validated drug combination and NOT clinical; 'drugged' = has a ChEMBL ligand; co-dependency correlation != SL (guarded structurally + by known-pair validation + two nulls). Cancer cell-line layer; not wet-lab, not response prediction. The 1% is a small but real dent in the 93% undrugged ceiling."
